{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-font-style:italic&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposal, in the absence of evidence pertaining to marketing, the needs of the\r\nlocal office market, or other evidence to demonstrate that the existing office use\r\ncan be considered to be surplus, redundant, or otherwise unsuitable for a use\r\nfalling within Use Class E(g), has failed to demonstrate compliance with Policy\r\nE1.E of the London Plan (2021) and Policy DM32.B of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Development Management\r\nPolicies Local Plan (2013). &amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0cm;text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span arial=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposal, due to the loss of the approved communal amenity area, would be detrimental to all future residential occupiers of the site. In addition, the proposed flat, by reason of the insufficient depth of its rear amenity space, the site circumstances to the front and rear of the proposed unit and the extent of glazing proposed, would result in an unacceptably poor quality of outlook and quality of private amenity space and an unreasonable degree of loss of privacy to the occupiers of the proposed unit, to the detriment of those future occupiers. The proposal is therefore contrary to policies&amp;nbsp;D6, and D3.D(7) of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS1.K of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012) and Policies DM1, DM25 and DM27 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
